   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Intro Music**: back after 62 archived shows (977 days); rare: 9 archived performances [11]\n- **Hot Fun In The Summertime**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Two Halves**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 13 archived performances [11]\n- **Hit It And Quit It**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- **Tyrone**: back after 117 archived shows (2276 days) [11]\n- **Cold Sweat**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [11]\n- **Get Down On It**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [11]\n- **Across 110th Street**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [11]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Evil Urges, Highly Suspicious, I'm Amazed, Touch Me I'm Going To Scream Pt. 1, Aluminum Park, Touch Me I'm Going To Scream Pt.2 [11]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2008-06-13.140v3.flacf16** (recommended): source not stated; 36 songs; 221 min; rated 4.89/5 by 9 [1]. Said about its sound: Audio quality is good despite rain interference affecting the recording; The recording is noted as one of the very well captured concerts [3][9]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Rain fell intermittently throughout the four-hour performance on the Which Stage [2]\n- Audience members danced and sang while standing in the rain [4]\n- The set ran from midnight until 3:45 a.m. on Saturday [6]\n- Rain hitting the microphone umbrella was audible during the performance [1]\n- Jeff Coffin joined the band on saxophone for this track [1]\n- Kirk Hammett appeared on guitar for this specific song [1]\n- Reviewer rates this as the best MMJ show they have ever heard [7]\n- Reviewer calls it the best My Morning Jacket show on the archive [8]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2008-06-13.140v3.flacf16**: taped by Brian Hadella; transferred by Brian Hadella; source: Neumann ak40 > lc3 > ka100 > km100 (FOB, 5' LOC, 7.5' up, NOS,) > Lunatec V3 > MTII (24/48) [1]",
